Full-Stack Docker Deployment Guide

React (Vite) + Express + Docker + Nginx

A full-stack web application built with **React, Vite, Node.js, Express.js, Nginx, Docker, and Docker Compose**.

This project was used as part of my **BuildLabs DevOps Internship – Task 1: Version Control & Containerization** to demonstrate practical knowledge of source control, Docker containerization, application networking, environment configuration, deployment, testing, and troubleshooting.


Project Overview

The application contains two main components:

* **Frontend:** React application built with Vite.
* **Backend:** Node.js REST API built with Express.js.

The frontend is compiled into static production files and served using **Nginx**.

The backend runs independently as an Express API.

Docker is used to package both components into containers, while Docker Compose manages the complete application.

 Main Components

text
client/              React + Vite frontend
server/              Express backend API
client/Dockerfile    Frontend container definition
server/Dockerfile    Backend container definition
client/nginx.conf    Nginx frontend and API proxy configuration
docker-compose.yml   Multi-container application configuration



Project Objective

The objective of this project is to prepare a web application for collaborative development and deployment using DevOps practices.

The task demonstrates:

* Git version control.
* GitHub repository management.
* Meaningful Git commits.
* Application containerization.
* Docker image creation.
* Docker Compose.
* Environment variables.
* Docker networking.
* Nginx reverse proxying.
* Application testing.
* Troubleshooting.
* Technical documentation.


